---
// Lesson 10.1e — 2-Button Jam: Polish
// rpg jam day: juice — feedback, sound, the 10-minute polishes.
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>10.1e — 2-Button Jam: Polish</h1>

<p class="lesson-lead">
    Polish is not decoration; it is COMMUNICATION AT 60 FPS. Every
    juice pass is the game answering the player's unasked questions:
    did that work? did it matter? can I do better? Today: sound,
    feedback, and the 30-second first impression — nothing new,
    everything better.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Polish Day</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~50 min</span>
    </div>

    <p><strong>The three passes (20 min each, from the wishlist
    ranked in <a href="10.1d.html">10.1d</a>):</strong></p>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>The 30-second first impression.</strong> A new
            player decides about your game in half a minute:
            what do they SEE first (a title screen IS your
            first screen — name it, color it), what do they
            DO first (a 5-second safe beat before the first
            threat — <a href="7.5.html">7.5</a> beat 1),
            what do they LEARN first (your two verbs, by
            doing them)?</li>
        <li><strong>Feedback on everything.</strong> Every action
            needs a visible/audible answer:
            <pre><code>verb pressed   → input feedback  (squash, flash, sound)
verb succeeded → reward         (coin sparkle, score pop)
verb failed    → consequence   (screen edge red, shake)
score gained   → number that MOVES (not a silent int)</code></pre>
            The starter taught you all of this:
            hit flashes (<a href="8.3.html">8.3</a>), coin
            destroy + count (<a href="2.1.html">2.1</a>),
            phase tints (<a href="8.2.html">8.2</a>). Reuse
            the tricks; they are yours.</li>
        <li><strong>Sound.</strong> Three sounds minimum: an
            action sound (verb), a gain sound (reward), a lose
            sound (fail). Free sources with real licenses
            (<a href="9.10.html">9.10</a> rules): Kenney.nl
            assets, freesound.org with CC filters. A jam game
            with three sounds beats a silent one with twenty
            mechanics.</li>
    </ol>

    <p><strong>Freeze rule:</strong> last 10 minutes = NO new
    changes. Build (File → Build Settings), run the BUILD, not the
    editor. Build bugs (missing scene in build list!) are tomorrow's
    showcase killers — find them today.</p>

</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Close of Day</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~5 min</span>
    </div>


    <div class="socratic">


        <h3>Socratic: Polish Is Communication</h3>


        <ol>


            <li>Every polish pass answers a question the player did not ask out loud — did that work, did it matter, can I do better. Which of your three answers is still missing?</li>


            <li>Which of the effects you added tells the player something — and which one you were tempted to add would only have been decoration?</li>


            <li>Someone plays your game for 30 seconds with no explanation. What do they know by second 30, and what do they still not know?</li>


        </ol>


    </div>



    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Show a 30-second first impression you designed</li>
            <li>Give every action feedback a tester can see or hear</li>
            <li>Ship three licensed sounds with credits in the repo</li>
            <li>Run a frozen BUILD — not the editor — before leaving</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-10/index.html">Unit 10: Jam Season</a> — juice and freeze rules</li>
        <li><a href="9.10.html">9.10 — Licenses</a> — sound sourcing rules</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next: <a href="10.1f.html">10.1f — 2-Button Jam: Showcase &amp; Retro</a></p>
</div>`;
---
<Lesson id="10.1e" title="10.1e 2-Button Jam: Polish — AP CS Principles" root=".." css="../style.css">
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Lesson>
